{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 136, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-output residual where none exists yields a large gain, whereas replacing an existing op gives smaller or negative change."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a useful 3x3 conv on edge 3 with skip loses capacity, so the edit's benefit is smaller than when it replaces none/weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Creating a new node2->output path adds capacity, which helps more than swapping out an avg_pool already there."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 absent node 2 often receives little or no input, so a conv on edge 5 contributes less."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the residual skip, removing the edge-0 conv cuts more of the cell's effective paths and hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 only feeds edge 2, edge 0 matters less, so removing it costs less accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a new short path from node 1 to output is beneficial, whereas replacing an existing op is neutral or harmful."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a strong 3x3 conv on an output-feeding edge with skip removes capacity, reducing the edit's effect."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why":